  "scope": "Ten statement-led derivations frozen before target release, followed by complete original/proposed comparisons. The group proves crossed defect, finite norm, cusp vanishing, direct all-Picard vanishing, Leray edge restriction, actual conductor nonvanishing, the full analytic all-Picard theorem, the local cusp obstruction, the analytic boundary cocycle and analytic support specialization. The preproof program uses exact Fraction linear algebra and coefficient-complete interpolation. The construction identity maps and nearby-cycle unit transport each cited primary input. IC replaces an unsupported converse with the proved implication; IH supplies the fixed-whisker selected vector lift and exact endpoint, and identifies the clockwise cusp orientation. IM records the primitive-generator map omega=epsilon*p*omega_AC without guessing epsilon. Frozen statements and derivations are preserved with dated qualifications; no extra independent credit is assigned to postrelease repairs.",
